From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] virtual: keep the jumbo holdback out of FEX's preferred band

The opt-in holdback (jumbo-mb) reserves its size at the top of the largest
free hole. On a device whose address space ends at 0x8000000000 that hole
is the top tail, so the holdback covers [0x7c00000000, 0x8000000000),
the band rpmalloc's selector tries first. Its other candidates lie below
64 GB, which such a device refuses, so any holdback there leaves FEX with
no band and x64 code cannot start. The hole walk now stops at
0x7c00000000; a device whose ceiling is at or below it is unchanged.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-25-witcher3-setup.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c b/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
index cff7b23..5453230 100644
--- a/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
+++ b/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
@@ -1958,6 +1958,23 @@ void ios_jumbo_holdback_init( void )
         ceiling = (unsigned long long)vmi.max_address;
     if (!ceiling) ceiling = 0x1000000000ull;
 
+    /* Playport: keep the holdback out of FEX's preferred host band.
+     *
+     * rpmalloc's band selector tries [0x7c00000000, 0x7fffffffff] first and
+     * runs only after this holdback exists. On a device whose ceiling is
+     * 0x8000000000 the largest hole is the top tail, so a holdback placed at
+     * its top covers that whole band. The selector's other candidates all lie
+     * below 64 GB, which such a device refuses (kr=3), so FEX would get no
+     * band at all ("ml755 FATAL: no FEX arena"). Cap the walk at the band's
+     * base instead. A device whose ceiling is at or below the band is
+     * unchanged. */
+    if (ceiling > 0x7c00000000ull)
+    {
+        dprintf( 2, "[jumbo-hold] ceiling 0x%llx capped at 0x7c00000000: the holdback stays "
+                 "below FEX's preferred band\n", ceiling );
+        ceiling = 0x7c00000000ull;
+    }
+
     /* largest free hole below the ceiling */
     while (addr < ceiling)
     {
